                  "name": "Story Paragraph",
                  "fill": "$text-muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "What if a space could tell you what's happening inside it — before you ever step through the door? Radar began as that question, scribbled on a whiteboard in the first hour of VTHacks 14.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.75,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 18,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "vHL4h",
                  "name": "Story Paragraph",
                  "fill": "$text-muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Over 36 hours we turned ordinary camera feeds into a live, top-down map. A vision model detects and tracks people and objects frame by frame; a lightweight server streams those detections to an interface that reads like a radar sweep — calm, glanceable, and honest about what it sees.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.75,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 18,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
